The GDN attention fix is a backport of upstream PR #34871:
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/34871
It is attributed to its upstream authors and is not claimed as a new fix here.

The token-rule encoder follows the bare/leading-space encoding approach used
by vLLM's bad_words processing. This project implements a different stopping
policy; it does not enable native bad_words logits masking.

Aho-Corasick is an established multi-pattern matching algorithm. No claim of
inventing the algorithm or of being the first streaming output guard is made.

Implementation, packaging, documentation and experiments used AI assistance.
This project is independent and is not an official vLLM project component.
